Sarah — all four go into the brief, not the review, and I've written them down as the constraints rather than as suggestions:

1. every exercise traceable to a clause the marking scheme actually has;
2. nothing testing behaviour the spec doesn't promise;
3. the autograder's cases stated in the brief, up front;
4. weighted so a half-solved part still scores — no all-or-nothing items.

That's the shape of the brief before I write a word of content, which is exactly the order it should be done in. 14:30 on the Monday is the log line and nobody's losing anything by it.

Priya — the autograder cases and the weighting are the two places to look hardest, per Sarah; noted.

Nothing else from me before Wednesday at 10:00.

— Mara
